Project Title: "DocuChat" – RAG-based Document Q&A System

Goal: Build a complete system where a user uploads a PDF and chats with it using AI.

Tech Stack: Python, LangChain, FastAPI, Streamlit, Vector DB (ChromaDB or FAISS).

Constraint: NO Jupyter Notebooks. All code must be written in modular .py files.

Phase 1: Project Setup & Structure
Objective: Learn how to set up a professional Python project structure.
Instructions:
Create a folder named DocuChat_Project.
Set up a virtual environment (python -m venv venv) and activate it.
Create a requirements.txt file (List libraries: fastapi, uvicorn, langchain, pypdf, faiss-cpu, streamlit, python-dotenv).
Create the following folder structure (do not put everything in one file):
Plaintext
DocuChat_Project/
├── app.py              # Streamlit Frontend
├── server.py           # FastAPI Backend
├── core/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── rag_pipeline.py # All LangChain logic goes here
│   └── utils.py        # Helper functions (file saving, etc.)
├── data/               # Folder to store uploaded PDFs temporarily
└── requirements.txt

Phase 2: The Logic Layer (core/rag_pipeline.py)
Objective: Build the RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) engine strictly using functions/classes, not cells.
Tasks:
Document Loading: Write a function load_pdf(file_path) using LangChain’s PyPDFLoader to extract text.
Splitting: Implement RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter to break text into chunks (e.g., chunk size 1000).
Vector Store: Create a function create_vector_db(chunks) that:
Takes text chunks.
Converts them to embeddings (Use HuggingFaceEmbeddings for free usage or OpenAIEmbeddings if you have API keys).
Stores them in a local Vector DB (FAISS or ChromaDB).
Retrieval Chain: Create a class RAGChatBot with a method get_answer(query).
It should retrieve the top 3 relevant chunks from the DB.
Feed them into an LLM (use LangChain’s ChatOpenAI or HuggingFaceHub).
Return the answer.

Phase 3: The API Layer (server.py)
Objective: Learn how to serve the ML logic via REST API.
Tasks:
Initialize FastAPI.
Create an endpoint POST /upload:
Accepts a PDF file upload.
Saves it to the data/ folder.
Triggers the "Vector Store" creation function from Phase 2.
Returns: {"message": "File processed successfully"}.
Create an endpoint POST /chat:
Accepts a JSON body: {"question": "What is the summary of page 5?"}.
Calls RAGChatBot.get_answer().
Returns: {"answer": "Here is the summary..."}.
Run the server using uvicorn server:app --reload.

Phase 4: The Frontend Layer (app.py)
Objective: Connect a frontend to the backend API (Simulating a real Full-Stack flow).
Tasks:
Use Streamlit to build a simple UI.
Sidebar: Add a file uploader widget.
When a file is uploaded, use Python's requests library to send it to the FastAPI POST /upload endpoint.
Main Chat Area:
Input box for the user to type a question.
When "Send" is clicked, hit the FastAPI POST /chat endpoint.
Display the AI's response in the chat window. 